  "finalText": "The new queue is empty. I triaged all 14 weekend tickets and two more (T-2015, T-2016) that arrived at 08:10 while I was working. Two of the 16 were closed as non-requests, three were merged away, and the other 11 are now open with a severity, deadline and assignee. Nobody was paged, and no tickets outside the queue were changed except T-1999, which I merged (see below).\n\n**Date check:** the task context said 2026-10-13, but the desk clock reads 2026-03-23 08:10Z, a Monday. I used the desk clock. The KB-55 amendment (2026-03-20 to 03-31) is in force on that date.\n\n**Closed as non-requests**\n- T-2010: SyncFlow marketing email.\n- T-2014: out-of-office auto-reply.\n\n**Merged duplicates**\n- **CRM search:** T-2005 was merged into T-2004. T-2004 is sev2 (crm, department), due 12:10, assigned to E-201 Ines Kovac. T-1990, the CSV export ticket, is a different defect per KB-24, so I left it alone.\n- **Payments builds:** T-2012 and T-1999 were merged into T-2003. T-2003 is sev2 (build-pipeline, department), assigned to E-101 Dana Whitfield, who was already on T-1999. It carries T-1999's 10:30 deadline, the earliest committed on any of the three.\n- **T-1999 was not a queue ticket.** It is the open CI alert for the same payments-service failure. Merging it into T-2003 was the only way to carry its earlier deadline onto the survivor.\n\n**Security**\n- T-2007 is a phishing report (the user typed a password into a fake page), so it is sev2 and owned by security-oncall. It is due 12:10 and assigned to E-601 Noor Haddad.\n\n**Other tickets**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Basis | Due (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2015 (payroll, department) | sev1 | matrix | 03-23 09:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 (payroll, single-user) | sev2 | KB-55 amendment | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2011 (payroll, team) | sev2 | matrix | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2013 (vpn, department) | sev2 | matrix | 03-23 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2001 (vpn, team) | sev3 | matrix | 03-23 17:00 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2002 (crm, single-user) | sev4 | matrix | 03-26 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei |\n| T-2008 (vpn, single-user) | sev4 | matrix | 03-26 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2016 (vpn, single-user) | sev4 | matrix | 03-26 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 (build-pipeline, single-user) | sev4 | matrix | 03-26 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n**Deadlines**\n- **Sev1 and sev2:** these run on the clock from the 08:10 triage time, so sev1 is +60 minutes and sev2 is +240 minutes.\n- **Sev3:** the desk opens at 09:00, so 480 business minutes ends at 17:00 the same day.\n- **Sev4:** 1,440 business minutes from 09:00 Monday, skipping the 03-25 holiday, ends at 17:00 on Thursday 03-26.\n\n**Cover**\n- The network-primary engineer, E-301 Yuki Sato, is on leave today. T-2001 and T-2013 therefore went to network-secondary's on-call engineer, E-303 Sanna Virtanen.\n- The business-apps engineer on call at 03-26 17:00, E-202 Tomas Lindqvist, is on leave that day. T-2002 therefore went to business-apps-secondary's E-203 Amara Osei.\n\n**Not done**\n- No ticket is company-wide, so there was no major incident and no runbook to run.\n- I did not escalate any ticket, because triage doesn't require it. T-2015 is sev1, so it could be escalated to incident-command if you want that.\n- T-2015 is a different problem from T-1997 (the bank export), so I didn't merge them.",
